<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56078" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατοπτρ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>show as in a mirror</i> or <i>by reflexion</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ-ίζοντος [τὴν ἶριν] ἀστέρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Placit.</u>
					3.5.11
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be mirrored</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				1609.19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>look into a mirror, behold oneself in it</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Zeno Stoic.
				1.66
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.48
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				15.687c
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>behold as in a mirror</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδέαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.107
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόξαν Κυρίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>2 Ep.Cor.</u>
					3.18
				</span></i>
			 (but here perh.<i>reflect</i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
